    "body": "Finding (local reproduction on `7e26134bf`):\n\n- 17 of the 18 tests: the post is still refused. The refusal text changed. The program sim now judges a box turned a quarter about Z (#2182, #2177). Thus the sim clause leads the refusal, for example `post blocked - gouge: program cuts below the model in 4695 cell(s), worst 3.00 mm`. The asserts that want the operation's own clause (\"C1: move ... cuts past the finish surface\", \"<op> now cuts part '<part>'\") fail.\n- 1 test shows an unsafe post: `stock_source_chamfer_refusal_names_cause_and_part_as_source_workaround`, case \"chamfer-rejudge-hint\". A stock-source 2D Chamfer into a part added after generation POSTS. The same case also posts with an aligned stock. This defect is older than #2182 (#1628). It is filed as #2308 (P1).\n\nCause: #2182 fixed four suites that used the quarter turn as the \"the sim does not judge\" device (`docs/decisions/2177-square-stock-sim.md`). Six other suites kept that device.\n\nFix plan: the six suites use the same device as #2182: a turn of 1e-6 rad about Z (`OBLIQUE`). Each \"held by the op\" check also asserts that the sim refuses that stock by name. No \"never posts\" assert is removed.\n",
